        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7ff57ff8-b1f4-5ec6-ad46-58add90da830",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: MV Bessel, Sorrento, Nicolo Martini\n- Companies: AG Weser\n- Places: Bremen, Portoscuso, Sardinia, Mediterranean Sea, Italy, Sicily, Cyprus\n- Topics: shipbuilding, ship renaming, shipwrecks, geography, autonomous regions\n\nFacts:\n- AG Weser built the cargo ship Sorrento in 1925 in Bremen for German owners.\n- The cargo ship Sorrento was later known as MV Bessel.\n- The ship was renamed Nicolo Martini in 1961.\n- Nicolo Martini served until 1972, when she ran aground at Portoscuso in Sardinia.\n- Sardinia is the second largest island in the Mediterranean Sea, after Sicily and before Cyprus.\n- Sardinia is an autonomous region of Italy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
